# Project Completion Policy

Goal: Complete the project by resolving implementation-scope blockers instead of
accumulating IN_PROGRESS tasks.

## Rule

1. Diagnose every blocker.
2. Classify it.

### A. Implementation blocker

Examples: missing API/UI/component, incorrect permission or routing, missing
migration, broken tests, failing build, accessibility/responsive gaps, stale
request bugs.

→ Implement the missing capability.
→ Add or update tests.
→ Verify.
→ Resume the original task.
→ Close the task if all acceptance criteria pass.

### B. Environmental blocker

Examples: no authorised test account/password available, missing Playwright
storageState, intentionally unavailable CI secrets, unknown production
credentials, unavailable third-party services.

→ Do not invent credentials, secrets, or external resources.
→ Do not weaken security to bypass the blocker.
→ Record the exact blocker.
→ Continue all remaining verifiable work.
→ Leave the task in the appropriate state until the environment is available.

## Notes

- Closure/audit-only prompts may temporarily forbid implementation; honour
  explicit user instructions over this policy when they conflict.
- Do not violate frozen project requirements, ADRs, or migration freezes to
  "complete" a task.
- Prefer fixing root causes that unblock verification (e.g. documented local
  seed accounts) when those are within accepted project scope.
